{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2126","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. G-C-D, Unlucky!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Two arrays $$$p$$$ and $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$ are given, where $$$p$$$ is the prefix GCD$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ of some array $$$a$$$, and $$$s$$$ is the suffix GCD of the same array $$$a$$$. In other words, if the array $$$a$$$ existed, then for each $$$1 \\le i \\le n$$$, the following equalities would hold both: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$p_i = \\gcd(a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_i)$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s_i = \\gcd(a_i, a_{i+1}, \\dots, a_n)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" Determine whether there exists such an array $$$a$$$ for which the given arrays $$$p$$$ and $$$s$$$ can be obtained."},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$$$$\\gcd(x, y)$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greatest_common_divisor"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"greatest common divisor (GCD)"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" of integers $$$x$$$ and $$$y$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of three lines:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 10^5$$$) — the length of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$p_1, p_2, \\dots, p_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq p_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$s_1, s_2, \\dots, s_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq s_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of all $$$n$$$ across all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) if there exists an array $$$a$$$ for which the given arrays $$$p$$$ and $$$s$$$ can be obtained, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"No"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may output each letter in any case (lowercase or uppercase). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be accepted as a positive answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n6\n72 24 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 6 12 144\n3\n1 2 3\n4 5 6\n5\n125 125 125 25 25\n25 25 25 25 75\n4\n123 421 282 251\n125 1981 239 223\n3\n124 521 125\n125 121 121\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the first test case, a possible array is: [$$$72,\\ 24,\\ 3,\\ 6,\\ 12,\\ 144$$$]."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the second test case, it can be shown that such arrays do not exist."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the third test case, there exists an array: [$$$125,\\ 125,\\ 125,\\ 25,\\ 75$$$]."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2126E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2126/problem/E"}